===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# A [[crafty]] but [[underhanded]] [[deception]].
#* {{quote-web|1=en|date=November 21, 2021|author=Charles Hugh Smith|work=When Everything Is Artifice and PR, Collapse Beckons|url=https://charleshughsmith.blogspot.com/2021/11/when-everything-is-artifice-and-pr.html|text=The notion that consequence can be as easily managed as PR is the ultimate '''artifice''' and the ultimate delusion.}}
# A [[trick]] played out as an [[ingenious]], but [[artful]], [[ruse]].
#* {{quote-web|en|date=2021-9-22|author=Caroline Siede|title=''{{w|Dear Evan Hansen}}'' is a misfire on just about every level|site=AV Club|url=https://www.avclub.com/dear-evan-hansen-is-a-misfire-on-just-about-every-level-1847718189|passage=The heightened worlds of darkly comedic satire and soapy high-school romance make it easy enough to roll with unrealistic casting choices—and that goes for stage musicals, too, where some level of '''artifice''' is built into the format.}}
# A [[strategic]] [[maneuver]] that uses some [[clever]] means to avoid [[detection]] or [[capture]].
# A [[tactical]] move to gain [[advantage]].
# {{lb|en|archaic}} Something made with technical skill; a [[contrivance]].

