===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# To [[construct]] by means of [[skill]] or specialised [[art]]
#* {{quote-book|en|title=The Modern Practice of American Machinists and Engineers {{...}}|url=https://books.google.com/books?id=lidWAAAAcAAJ|author=Egbert Pomroy Watson|year=1867|passage=The Creator has so cunningly endowed our bodies that there is no labor to be done, no skill in '''artificing''' or fashioning the metals, that is beyond our reach.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|journal=Country Life|volume=7|page=138|url=https://books.google.com/books?id=_UIxAQAAMAAJ|year=1900|passage=Some of the greatest artists of their day either furnished designs or with their own hands '''artificed''' ornaments for domestic use,}}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=The A.M.C. White Mountain Guide: A Guide to Trails in the Mountains|url=https://books.google.com/books?id=DJ8SAAAAYAAJ|author=Appalachian Mountain Club|year=1922|passage=Splints and slings, already described, are easily '''artificed''' out of small saplings or from stiff bark.}}

